The number of triangles in the given figure is shown below:

 [IMAGE: https://cdn.repeatermock.com/tb/d8d00f8dc5f724b13d38923a901e7e2d0db4af7f6265b9ad80109434d585fa39.png] 

Number of triangles at the base line = 3

Formula Used = {n(n + 2)(2n + 1)over 8}

Where; n = 3

So,

Number of triangles = {3(3 + 2)(2 times 3 + 1)over 8}

= {3(3 + 2)(6 + 1)over 8}

= {3 times 5 times 7over 8}

= 13.125 ≈ **13**

Thus, there are a total of 13 triangles.

Hence, "Option 3" is the correct answer.
